{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551503-toronto","id":551503,"title":"Toronto","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-12T08:10:03-07:00","id":551503,"title":"Toronto","content":"I just posted Court Creation and Toronto. This thread is for discussing Toronto.<br /> <br /> This is the post: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-court-creation-and-toronto/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-th...n-and-toronto/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:55:27-07:00","id":551740,"title":"","content":"Obligatory MY CITY<br /> <br /> Toronto's an interesting choice for a freehold, but I've always maintained that it'd be an interesting one.<br /> <br /> If anything, the Courts of Toronto could be more fractious - there are so many different perspectives that you could view Toronto with. I wish there had been a bit more focus on the suburbs of Toronto, which are a very big part of the city, and where the outlook changes significantly.<br /> <br /> It's also pretty cool knowing that I live next to one of the biggest Goblin Markets in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5408-fetfet","name":"fetfet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5408_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:03:13-07:00","id":551752,"title":"","content":"Surprised Yonge Street got a paragraph, but Casa Loma, the fairy-tale folly house, didn't. The CN tower description is awesome, and Kensington the Goblin Market is too obvious NOT to use, so that's awesome. <br /> Other than that, I think it does my hometown justice. The theme of multiculturalism is strong here (Diversity Our Strength and all that), which I like. Other themes in the city that aren't as stressed are the themes of &quot;Toronto the Good&quot;, domineeringly moralistic Toronto, and of the 416-905 divide, the great socio-political divide between the Old City of Toronto and the outer regions annexed to Toronto in the Amalgamation. This divide pretty much defines all modern political struggles in Toronto, and the vast majority of major political debates in City Hall can easily map to the liberal Old City versus the conservative suburbs, often meaning that, for example, City Council decides to rebuild a raised highway running through downtown Toronto based against the votes of every councillor whose wards are anywhere near the highway. <br /> Those themes may be themes better explored in other games, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:14:50-07:00","id":551789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551503-toronto?p=551752#post551752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surprised Yonge Street got a paragraph, but Casa Loma, the fairy-tale folly house, didn't. The CN tower description is awesome, and Kensington the Goblin Market is too obvious NOT to use, so that's awesome.<br /> Other than that, I think it does my hometown justice. The theme of multiculturalism is strong here (Diversity Our Strength and all that), which I like. Other themes in the city that aren't as stressed are the themes of &quot;Toronto the Good&quot;, domineeringly moralistic Toronto, and of the 416-905 divide, the great socio-political divide between the Old City of Toronto and the outer regions annexed to Toronto in the Amalgamation. This divide pretty much defines all modern political struggles in Toronto, and the vast majority of major political debates in City Hall can easily map to the liberal Old City versus the conservative suburbs, often meaning that, for example, City Council decides to rebuild a raised highway running through downtown Toronto based against the votes of every councillor whose wards are anywhere near the highway.<br /> Those themes may be themes better explored in other games, however.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I forgot about Casa Loma! For that matter, there's a lot of architecture at the University of Toronto that's pretty fairy-tale. I guess it was space concerns?<br /> <br /> I was also concerned about the 416-905 divide, it's kinda what I was getting at. But I think the Sheherezade Freehold is about transcending those kinds of spacial limitations, and focusing more on the people, now that I read it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5408-fetfet","name":"fetfet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5408_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:24:02-07:00","id":551812,"title":"","content":"The suburb demographics is actually more multicultural than the downtown, even if us downtowners pride ourselves more in multiculturalism, it's just more patchwork than mosaic: large patches of various groups all living in close-knit proximity, rather than the more scattered mosaic of downtown. I mean, thing of Somali Torontonians, they almost all live in one neighbourhood!<br /> <br /> Edit: either way, I think it does a better job than the Vampire:tR 1.0 attempt at it, can't remember which book it was in, it featured Casa Loma heavily but it felt like you could do the same sort of city anywhere. A good example city should be unique to the city it's in, and I think this pulls that off fairly well.<br /> <br /> Edit Edit: So which Court helped found the Aga Khan Museum and Ismaili Cultural Centre? Brass or Ivory? Either would work, and given that Toronto doesn't have a HUGE Middle eastern population (not in proportion to it's Indian or Chinese populations), I would bet that the recent opening and ridiculous awesomeness of the Museum was an inspiration for the Brass Court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","user":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","date":". 06-12-2015, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:26:08-07:00","id":551815,"title":"","content":"David, I could frigging kiss you! As I've said in other threads, I'm always jonesing for more Canadian stuff from the World of Darkness, although Toronto isn't my first choice since I've had limited contact with it, that's okay because it is a good fit for changeling. Even better is that you not only picked up on Arabian/Islamic themes, you specifically went for Iranian inspiration, which is one of the areas my history degree is focused on (never mind that I live across the Gulf from Iran right now anyhow). I was super excited to read this and it did not disappoint. I like that you picked a premise that most people will be familiar with to be accessible while giving plenty of options for the Iranian slat to it, but also leaving the Courts open to other cultures as well. The Court of Jade in particular was a nice touch, and now I'm having to think up ways to intertwine Smaug with a Lung Dragon for their court symbol. Overall awesome job!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:44:32-07:00","id":551831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551503-toronto?p=551812#post551812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The suburb demographics is actually more multicultural than the downtown, even if us downtowners pride ourselves more in multiculturalism, it's just more patchwork than mosaic: large patches of various groups all living in close-knit proximity, rather than the more scattered mosaic of downtown. I mean, thing of Somali Torontonians, they almost all live in one neighbourhood!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely true. I think that the Courts went a ways to outline that demographic, but there could be more here. Regardless, it's an incredible view of Toronto, and I'm happy to see my city(!) done justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5408-fetfet","name":"fetfet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5408_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:35:05-07:00","id":551887,"title":"","content":"I really love that Freehold, with the Silver Court being my personal favorite- the way it was formed is really interesting, and I always loved those kinds of groups :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T13:19:13-07:00","id":552070,"title":"","content":"I've never been to Toronto, so I can't vouch for accuracy or if it &quot;captured the spirit&quot; of the city, but I really liked this write-up. It builds an interesting setting and gives some good ideas on what to do with a setting/Chronicle of your own, which I feel are exactly what the setting sections are supposed to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T18:50:05-07:00","id":552445,"title":"","content":"I like this quite a lot. All the Courts are awesome, and I'd love to play almost all of them, though my favorite is the Brass Court(Shocker, I know! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), and I wouldn't be too heartbroken even if I had to play Ivory. <br /> <br /> Anyone else think it'd be fun to play a Courtless campaign themed around discovering the truth about Ruby and reforming/redeeming the Court?<br /> <br /> Also, is the lack of what the 2nd Mantle dot is a Goblin Vow with intentional or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T19:26:39-07:00","id":552483,"title":"","content":"I'm with Illuminated Minutia: while not at all familiar with Toronto, I think this is a really cool setting writeup. ^_^ There are a lot of good hooks in place, and it gives a helpful structure to playing in and interacting with this Freehold and its Courts, as well as inspiring ideas in building one's own Court system.<br /> <br /> Were I to pick a favorite, I'd probably go with the Brass Court. I don't think I'd have considered having the highest rank serve as a chief adviser to the Freehold's ruler or creating a student-teacher relationship across most of the other Titles, but those are really awesome components. I feel they really convey the spirit of the Court. I also enjoyed the clarity around Faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551503-toronto?p=552445#post552445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is the lack of what the 2nd Mantle dot is a Goblin Vow with intentional or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good question. I'd forgotten that the Court creation example specified Goblin Vow (mines) for the Copper Court. Perhaps David's waiting to fill in some parts of the Court write-ups until the Contracts and Goblin Vows section is complete?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T21:38:55-07:00","id":552533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551503-toronto?p=552483#post552483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good question. I'd forgotten that the Court creation example specified Goblin Vow (mines) for the Copper Court. Perhaps David's waiting to fill in some parts of the Court write-ups until the Contracts and Goblin Vows section is complete?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, it's an issue with merging drafts, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T00:59:54-07:00","id":552682,"title":"","content":"Having caught up with this I like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would like more details on why the Freeholds were fighting. I'd imagine that attacking another Freehold's Bulwark is against the &quot;Changeling Geneeva convention&quot; so I'd expect there to be a big reason - however it mostly came across as &quot;they had different cultures in one area, so thus they fight&quot;. Why were they at war and not just living and let living?<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing that caught my eye. Some of the Approaches require direct interaction between the Changeling and the Huntsman, like Brass' Foundations of Sand. Other's like Jade's Mortal Influence I can't imagine going any other way than the Storyteller declaring off screen that a Huntsman has talked the police into raiding the Changeling. Once SWAT are knocking at the door you've already got that point of Yearning.<br /> <br /> Is that intentional? Should it say that you get a chance to defend yourself from the mortals first?<br /> <br /> <br /> One very cool thing about Brass; is that (AFAIK) in Islamic mythology the Djinn are said to be able to accept Islam, in Christian folklore faeries are said to feel pain just from hearing the word Jesus. That little contrast is cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T10:22:25-07:00","id":553181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551503-toronto?p=552070#post552070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been to Toronto, so I can't vouch for accuracy or if it &quot;captured the spirit&quot; of the city, but I really liked this write-up. It builds an interesting setting and gives some good ideas on what to do with a setting/Chronicle of your own, which I feel are exactly what the setting sections are supposed to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Torontonians just like to talk about themselves. We're vain, self-important people. One of Toronto's nicknames is the Centre of the Universe.<br /> <br /> And there are really interesting parallels to real events in the Courts. The formation of the Silver Court is similar to the amalgamation of Toronto, which incorporated several suburbs into the city proper. It's just a great write-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5408-fetfet","name":"fetfet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5408_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:31:59-07:00","id":554563,"title":"","content":"I could see the Sultina's Freehold extending across the GTA, From Toronto's Water front, to Newmarket at the Northern end of the GTA.<br /> <br /> Toronto Freehold sounds big. <br /> <br /> Some thoughts, given the description of the Ivory court I'm not sure how it connects to Greed, its primarily based on creating a cult that worships the changeling members of the ivory court.<br /> <br /> I'm Adjulation/Adoration makes more sense then Greed, I mean look at the emotion they're most likely to engender. <br /> <br /> I still love the court, and I can see synergy with Lost Pantheon entitlement. The Cult of Mitra merits are cool as well, but if you max out Cult of Mitra and Ivory Mantle you can end up with 2 or three retainers.<br /> <br /> All the courts seem really cool including the lost court, the Ruby Court, and you can also use Seasonal and Seelie Courts as advesaries or forgien allies of the Silver Court.<br /> <br /> The Silver Court is a mix of all the Seasonal Courts and the Seelie Courts, focuses on the emotion of only one, Wrath. Maybe I suggest the emotion of conflicted, the emotion one has when one is feeling competing emotions. I feel conflicted. Alternately Bloodthirsty/Sadistic would work as well, since it touches upon the other courts.<br /> <br /> Jades Court is really cool as well, Chinese in primary origin, but adapting to Multiculturalism and the need to include other cultures in order to expand. In fact all have element of that, such as an ivory courtier of Europeon extraction focusing on a more Hellenistic Mithras for example.<br /> <br /> Brass is cool because while you have a majority of Muslims, you could also have Hindu members, Deeply Christian members, Wiccans (although most would be more attracted to Silver Court and Herne), Political Activists deeply devoted to an idealogy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T11:27:03-07:00","id":554612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551503-toronto?p=554563#post554563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Some thoughts, given the description of the Ivory court I'm not sure how it connects to Greed, its primarily based on creating a cult that worships the changeling members of the ivory</div> </div> </div> </div> The cult, as I understand it, is a means to a ends. What matters is that the cult is useful, allow the &quot;gods&quot; to use their servants for resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T18:54:31-07:00","id":555099,"title":"","content":"The other stuff mentioned is small stuff, but one bigger thing is while they're are Jade Court (high Asian Influence), Ivory Court (high East Indian/Persian with some Grecoroman influence), Middle East Influence, Silver Court European Influence predominately, there is no AfroCaribean influenced Court. <br /> <br /> I do understand that eacb of these Courts have expanded to be more multicultural themselves, but its a starting point.<br /> <br /> Maybe tomorrow I'll provide story hooks for TO and ideas as to what areas would fit which courts within the GTA, for example Bay Street would likely be Ivory Court turf. Others even more experienced then me can provide more. <br /> <br /> Toronto has three big parades, Santa Claus Parade, Gay Pride, and Caribana, in fact the biggest Carabana Parade outside Trinda and Tabago I belive, so I think maybe Gold Court, perhaps based on the Festive/Celebatory emotion would be awesome for the Toronto Court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 06-14-2015, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T19:11:36-07:00","id":555103,"title":"","content":"So many plot hooks, I can see some Monarchs of the Jade Court having ambitions to become a Courts in they're own rights for example, Members of the Silver Court being secretly spies for seasonal and seelie courts, the Ivory Court having connections to Hunters (heck the Cult of Mitra is practically a Hunter Conspiracy, hunting the Huntsmen in beautiful irony), or even Guardian's of the Veill Cults or Mummy Cults (or rivals for mortal worshippers). Then there is the Court of Brass' connection with that lion headed bird, what is it, where did it come from and why is it interested in the Court of Brass (I assume its a Hobgoblin). This is in addition to the regular threats from Loyalists, Fetches, Huntsmen).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T23:24:00-07:00","id":555354,"title":"","content":"I'm more interested in Scheherazade Freehold itself - as I understand a story, a model of it comes from Persian Freehold that fell, when last sultan of it could not commerce Bulwark ( i.e. tell new story ) and Fae raid the city. he run away to Canada and started new Freehold in Toronto.<br /> <br /> So in Persia there is still similar, &quot;sister&quot; Scheherazade Freehold? But I would assume they have different Courts Model in there, even if Bulwark is the same.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T00:26:03-07:00","id":555372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551503-toronto?p=555354#post555354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more interested in Scheherazade Freehold itself - as I understand a story, a model of it comes from Persian Freehold that fell, when last sultan of it could not commerce Bulwark ( i.e. tell new story ) and Fae raid the city. he run away to Canada and started new Freehold in Toronto.<br /> <br /> So in Persia there is still similar, &quot;sister&quot; Scheherazade Freehold? But I would assume they have different Courts Model in there, even if Bulwark is the same.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not quite. The Scheherazade of the time foresaw the Iranian Revolution and that it would shatter the freehold. So the entire thing picked up and travelled through the Hedge to Canada. There is no more freehold in Iran anymore, or if there is, its a brand new tradition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T02:49:51-07:00","id":555429,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the new Courts are under the authority of the Anatolla of Iran, with all use of Fae Magic concidered anti Islamic, and banned, which would leave the Persian and Arab Changelings vulnerible to the Huntsmen and other mystical predators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T03:40:04-07:00","id":555439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551503-toronto?p=555429#post555429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the new Courts are under the authority of the Anatolla of Iran, with all use of Fae Magic concidered anti Islamic, and banned, which would leave the Persian and Arab Changelings vulnerible to the Huntsmen and other mystical predators.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but I think we can be more creative than that. Nothing against you, but I've seen a general trend in Modern Fantasy to cast Islam as the anti-magic religion, and I'm getting very tired of it. Given that many of the metaphysics and mystical concepts that originate with Muslim philosophers and scholars, that seems very unfair to me. Likewise, having studied the History of Islam and lived in the Middle East for the last three years, I see no reason to cast any of the countries I've visited as being more or less receptive to magic than in the West.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd start from a similar premise, but go in a very different direction. Sorry if I go into teacher mode for a bit.<br /> <br /> Changelings have a very legalist style of magic and that is very resonant with Islamic concepts. Ayatollah isn't actually a specifically Iranian term, it refers to high ranking legal scholars of Twelver Shiism (Iran's majority religions) and is often mixed up with the Supreme Leader, or Guardian Jurist, because the Leader of Iran's Revolution, Ruhollah Khomeini, was himself one of many Ayatollahs. I'd argue it would be far more interesting to have the Freehold of Iran, born after the Revolution and the excess Hunting of the True Fae, be servants of the Guardian Jurist but almost be like a secret branch of the government, investigating and securing the revolution against paranormal threats, especially if they get directed towards the Guardian Jurist himself.<br /> <br /> I don't know, I'd have to do more research to find a way to make it fit with modern Iranian history and culture, but that seems much more interesting to me personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 06-15-2015, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T04:28:36-07:00","id":555466,"title":"","content":"I wasn't refering to the whole Islamic world, but rather the current regime. which I thought would provide an interesting contrast with the beliefs of the Muslim members of the Toronto Freehold.<br /> <br /> I'm not as familiar Islam as you I admit, when it comes to Muslim mystism I'm only heard of the Sufi's. I once saw a Sufi take an axe to the head in a documentary as if it was nothing, it was cool and badass. <br /> <br /> I will note that the Toronto Changeling Muslims seem to have they own variation of Islam, just as Christian Vampires have they're own domination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T05:24:31-07:00","id":555511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551503-toronto?p=555466#post555466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't refering to the whole Islamic world, but rather the current regime. which I thought would provide an interesting contrast with the beliefs of the Muslim members of the Toronto Freehold.<br /> <br /> I'm not as familiar Islam as you I admit, when it comes to Muslim mystism I'm only heard of the Sufi's. I once saw a Sufi take an axe to the head in a documentary as if it was nothing, it was cool and badass. <br /> <br /> I will note that the Toronto Changeling Muslims seem to have they own variation of Islam, just as Christian Vampires have they're own domination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, and I know you aren't trying to speak for all of the Muslim world. It does set up a good contrast, the way you've done it doesn't seem to resonate with me. I think it may be because Mordern Iran always gets portrayed as completely oppressive in all forms of media, so I feel fatigued when it gets brought up. Don't get me wrong, there's a reason for that stereotype, but there are many ways it gets broken too. My favourite on is that while homosexuality is illegal, gender reassignment surgeries are state-funded, which is not something that is common in any country. Little quirks like that give you a sense of depth to the country, so I feel like the narrative of the Freehold is better served by a group of changeling that is thought of as being very Islamic rather than unIslamic. Vampires on the other hand...<br /> <br /> But to each their own <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If that's what you want to run with, I won't stop you. I just feel very passionate about this, and needed to explain myself,<br /> <br /> I wouldn't really equate the Toronto Freehold with a variant Islam. Everything Islamic in the document seems to be fairly mainstream, and then what you actually see is a plurality of cultures and beliefs. And all of it, all of it, is glorious. Hamdullah!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:45:52-07:00","id":555851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551503-toronto?p=555372#post555372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite. The Scheherazade of the time foresaw the Iranian Revolution and that it would shatter the freehold. So the entire thing picked up and travelled through the Hedge to Canada. There is no more freehold in Iran anymore, or if there is, its a brand new tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so answer me this - what history started 200 years ago? Toronto's or Esfahan, Persia? Because it's wierd for me that <b>1001 Nights original Freehold would be only 200 years old</b> - as the book itself is at least 1000 years old.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toronto Freehold Preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The freehold's story begins over two hundred years ago in far away Esfahan, Persia. It begins with a foolish Shah whose pride shattered his freehold's Bulwark and brought a djinn and his huntsmen down upon them. Scheherazade* the cleverest and fairest of the Brass Court* went out to face them alone. As the story goes, she told them a tale and when the sun rose offered them hospitality within her lamp. Each night she told them a new story and each day they rest within the magic lamp.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T11:43:57-07:00","id":555880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551503-toronto?p=555851#post555851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so answer me this - what history started 200 years ago? Toronto's or Esfahan, Persia? Because it's wierd for me that <b>1001 Nights original Freehold would be only 200 years old</b> - as the book itself is at least 1000 years old.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toronto Freehold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whether the story is true or not is the subject of debate within the freehold's courts, but the ritual of telling a new story each night- not one that any Scheherazade has ever told before- is the freehold's Bulwark against the True Fae.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>To me, the text is fairly clear that the Freehold was around 200 years ago in Esfahan, then migrated to Toronto before the Revolution. Whether or not they have the actual truth behind the story of 1001 Arabian Nights is questionable, especially since those stories can be traced back to Persian and Sanskrit texts, particularly the <i>Haz\u0101r Afs\u0101n</i> which places some of them, including the framing device, more on the level of 2000 years old. What matters isn't the historical truth. What matters is the Bulwark and the telling of the tales. <br /> <br /> Now my personal reading of this is that some changelings had an experience that was similar to the Tale of the City of Brass, and experienced things similar <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scheherazade's </span></span>similar own tale. They were able to build their Bulwark around that. That's only one reading though, so if you want to go with something else, by all means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T20:52:12-07:00","id":556444,"title":"","content":"Actually I have heard that Iran is not as oppressive as the Western Media makes it out to be, I mean people say things like women aren't allowed to wear make up, but then how the heck did Iran come one of the largest markets of not just makeup, but comesmetic surgery as well. There is a high rate of education and that's just the beginning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T02:18:52-07:00","id":556700,"title":"","content":"I'm ending reading Courts section and I must say i generally like the &quot;culture-based&quot; Courts of Toronto, with their own ethnicity stories as part of Scheherazade Tale. At least till I go to the Silver Court. <br /> <br /> The &quot;European&quot; Court is based on merging of Seasonal and Seelie/Unseelie Courts - but it's, in reality, the Summer Court with different image. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do not feel in Silver Courts a real merger of at least Summer and Autumn, not to mentioned other groups from what it should hail from. Does it should not have somehow similar structure to the Jade Court, with multiple Monarchs, only working in tandem? Or maybe sharing the Crown between Seasons? But the worst is Emotion - why Wrath only? The &quot;White&quot; Changelings need to be associated only with violence? Especially as other Courts have more stoic emotions - Faith, Pride, Greed. So <b>why</b> Silver Court have Wrath? It's also illogical with symbology connection - when Silver is connected with violance? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T06:41:17-07:00","id":556844,"title":"","content":"Because Wrath is what they took from the Summer Court when they seized the story of the Wild Hunt, and from each of the others they took something else that shaped their identity as the Silver Court. It's explained right there.<br /> <br /> And if that's not enough for you, how about you use your<i> imagination</i>? Maybe there were more Summer courtiers left than of Spring or Winter, or even Autumn and both Seelie and Unseelie, so the image of the new court their remains created has stronger Summer influence.<br /> <br /> It's also a court created to consolidate several different ideas to ensure they would all survive, so I wouldn't expect its overall theme to be as focused or cohesive as the other courts of Toronto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-16-2015, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T10:43:06-07:00","id":557053,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking they should be more be Summer-Autumn alliance more, not mostly Summer clone...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:08:00-07:00","id":559983,"title":"","content":"Silver is associated with fighting Werewolves, but otherwise I don't know. <br /> <br /> I do agree about Wrath being the court emotion unbalances things in favour of Summer, especially since the general vibe leans abit towards summer already, although it does include symbols of other courts.<br /> <br /> I think I have the perfect emotion for the Silver Court, Aggression. It fits the theme of the wild hunt, its related to all the other courts emotions. Wrath usually leads to Aggression if not unchecked, Aggression acted upon can cause fear, Desire can be enhanced by Aggressive feeling in the right situation (S&amp;M), and Sadness can be the result of acting carelessly on the emotion of Agression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:28:01-07:00","id":560029,"title":"","content":"I'm really curious about the Court Contracts, Emotion likely to be mostly about inflicting, manipulating, and dispeling a particular emotion, but they're maybe a twist to it somewhere. <br /> <br /> Talespinning, perhaps related to the Freehold's story and/or using tales to warp reality some how? <br /> <br /> I wonder if XX is the same contract for all the courts in a Freehold or Unique to each Court?<br /> <br /> And do Court Contracts have Seeming bonuses like Universal Contracts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:06:15-07:00","id":560264,"title":"","content":"The Toronto Courts have inspired an idea for a Character. <br /> <br /> This has inspired an idea for a character, Shadowsand, a former Oilsands worker who moved to Alberta from Toronto for a high paying job in the Oilsands, but ended up in Arcadia instead, upon espacing he left Alberta for Toronto when he decided that his fetch had done something more meaningful with his life then Joe Barolski (Shadowsands) had.<br /> <br /> Joe is a Sandharrow Darkling whose mien makes him look like he's made of Oilsands. He advanced up the ranks of the Ivory Court, which warped his mien, thick streaks of gold dust in intricate patterns criss cross his body, making him look alitte less creepy, and a little cooler. His eyes are like glowing emaralds, and he smells faintly of bullshit. everything within a few feet of Joe seems to be covered faintly in gold and Ivory dust. Shandowsand has ***** Mantle Merits in the Ivory Court.<br /> <br /> Shadowsand is a Mitrae within the Cult of Mitra by day, but by night he helps manage the trinity clubs in missaguaga, stripclubs famed for they're &quot;extras&quot;. He uses the clubs as recruitment centres for the Cult of Mitra.<br /> <br /> Shadowsand's enemies call him Bitamen Joe behind his back, which pisses him off to no end. He's put his Oil days behind him and he doesn't like reminders. <br /> <br /> So we know Shadowsand can regain a point of clarity for.doing something morally questionable on behalf of someone else if they think it has to be done, or risk losing a point for blind trust, we know as a Sandharrow he gets +2 to grapple checks, and can use less solid to slip through tiny finger sized holes, +2 to armour, and can apply armour to defence. Those trying to lie to him get -1 to they're rolls, he gets a goblin vow merit related to the Ivory Court, he gets to reroll 9 on Persausian rolls, a new personal approach, and a *** retainer and once per story can use ***** dots of retainers, allies, or resources from the cult of Mitra. He can spend a glamour to release himself from restraints, enter dreams of nearby sleeping people, enter the hedge, go into the hedge into order to enter someones dreams physically, can harvest glamour, make pledges, use Wyrd as a defence against magic, use ***** Mantle as bonus dice in rolls in reguards to Ivory Court Members, gain the Darkling Seeming bonus on any contract he gains that has said bonus, can apply mantle to rolls to resist the True Fey (I don't know if this includes they're servants) as long as the Bulwork is still up. <br /> <br /> Work in Progress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 06-19-2015, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T04:10:46-07:00","id":563945,"title":"","content":"I wonder how the Fae Touched fit into Toronto, I'm inclined to think they're an accepted members of the Courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T04:45:32-07:00","id":563974,"title":"","content":"It's amazing how close some of my own ideas for an Arabian Court system are to this.<br /> <br /> May need to come up with something that connects the displaced Persian Scheherazade Court to the also-1001 Nights tied Courts of Baghdad (specifically dating all the way back to the days of Harun al-Rashid).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-22-2015, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T06:32:11-07:00","id":565338,"title":"","content":"Some cool places in Toronto are ripply's believe it or not aquarium beside the CN Tower between the CN Tower and the Sky Dome. I'd personally add the Skydome and Ripply's to the hedge. Actually because they're so close together, it makes the Skydome look kind of like a set of testicles beside the very phallic CN Tower. Cool thing to note about CN is that while it has a resturant and entertainment facialities, its also transmits signals like over the air TV stations, bet you'd get some interesting channels in the hedge.<br /> <br /> Younge Street is the longest street in the world (I don't care what the haters say), on it you can find just about anything.<br /> <br /> On young street you can find a stripclub called the Brass Rail, it was the stripclub used in American Pie: Beta House. It has a rep for being a tourist trap. <br /> <br /> Toronto used be filled with stripclubs, but there aren't that many anymore, they've given way to Massage Parlours and Escorts, because who doesn't like a happy ending (fairy tale or otherwise). Some of the remaining stripclubs like Fairbanks, and the Trinity Clubs in Missauga (Cafe Alantis, Midway Invader, and one other I think) are extras heavy and may lean towards being brothels at times. <br /> <br /> Toronto's Entertain district is being ruined by idiots you think its a good place to build condos, and complaints from said idiots have driven some club owners out of business. The last Superclub in TO closed its doors rescently.<br /> <br /> Toronto sits on one of the Great Lakes (they're practically fresh water seas. Toronto even extends onto islands in Lake Ontario. <br /> <br /> Former Mayor Ford, best known for his crack piper and buckets of chicken and weird obsession with Toronto's Gravy, really put Toronto on the Map and would make a really good Changeling NPC character in any chronicle.<br /> <br /> Areas in the wider GTA are York Region, where I live, made up the towns/cities of Richmond Hill, Newmarket, Aurora, Markham, Whitechurch-Stouffville, King, Vaughan, Geogina, East Gwillenbury.<br /> <br /> My favour parts of this area are Newmarket with Upper Canada Mall, Concord area of Thornhill (which I think is part of Richmond Hill), because it has the Whiskey A-Go-Go stripclub and right beside it Vaughan Spa (adult entertainment) or as I like to call it my happy place. Blondie's Spa is also nearby is by. I also like Wilcox Lake in Oakridges (part of Richmond Hill). Newmarket also has Fairy Lake, how perfect for Changeling, which has trails all over the place with pretty street lights.<br /> <br /> Scarbough another part of Toronto proper is the inspiration for the movie Wayne's World. I do some business from time to time in Scarbrough.<br /> <br /> Missauga was governed for ever and a day by Mayor Hazel McCallun aka Hurricane Hazel because she was politically invincible, she'd been Mayor for longer then Missauga has existed in its current form, he'd just retire in the last municiple elections, much beloved, another good potential changeling NPC.<br /> <br /> Major Parades include the Santa Claus Parade, which gets televised all over the world, both on the internet and to television stations across the globe.<br /> <br /> Toronto has the largest Carabana Parade outside Trinidad and Tobago I believe, its a huge celebrantion of diversity. Colours, feathers, and all kinds of stuff, its perfect for Changeling.<br /> <br /> Gay Pride Parade is huge in Toronto, gets tourists from around the world.<br /> <br /> Slut Walk I think Toronto might be were it originated, not sure, cheaper then a stripclub, but be advised not to bring a sign suggesting you don't believe in rape culture, reporter and libertarian candiate Lauren Southern almost got lynched at the slut walk for doing that. <br /> <br /> Taste of the Danforth, big foodie thing on the Danforth.<br /> <br /> NDP leader Tom Mulcair has said Toronto is the most important city in Canada, which is ballsy because Tom Mulcair represents a riding in Montreal, and Toronto and Montreal have rivalry, although Toronto does have a large Habs fans community, mostly Montrealers who got fed up with the xenophobia of the seperatist movement in Quebec so moved to Toronto.<br /> <br /> Toronto is the capital of Ontario, a Pronvince bigger then most European Countries. We call the legislature Queen's Park.<br /> <br /> Toronto is also the setting of Lost Girl TV show and Murdoch Mysteries.<br /> <br /> Bay street is the capital of Canada's finance industry, its like Canada's Wall Street, it would definately be Ivory Court terroritory. The Toronto Stock Exchange, aka the TSX is Canada's largest.<br /> <br /> GTA, Greater Toronto Area, has a larger population then most provonces within Canada. I think only Ontario, Quebec, and BC have a larger population.<br /> <br /> Lots of other fun stuff in Toronto. I'll add anything I can think of later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T06:55:51-07:00","id":565356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_Toronto_Area\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Vaughan_Metropolitan_Centre_Skyline%2C_August_7_2025.jpg/1280px-Vaughan_Metropolitan_Centre_Skyline%2C_August_7_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_Toronto_Area\" target=\"_blank\"> Greater Toronto Area - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_Toronto_Area\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_Toronto_Area </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I knew York Region and Peel Region were part of GTA, but I didn't realize Durham and Halton Region were as well. The Greater Toronto Area has a population of over 6,000,000 people, even if there is one Changeling for every 10,000 people that's over 600 changelings, if its 1 changeling for every 1000 people, that means over 6,000 changelings in the GTA!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T07:13:33-07:00","id":565369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.greatertoronto.org/why-greater-toronto/economic-overview/population\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.greatertoronto.org/why-greater-toronto/images/pixel_line.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <di